```

**Why this works:** `showModal()` opens the dialog in the top layer — above every other element regardless of z-index — makes the rest of the page inert (unfocusable, unclickable), traps Tab focus inside the dialog, and wires up the Escape key for free. These are the three hardest parts of DIY modals, solved natively. The backdrop-click trick works because the `::backdrop` is part of the dialog element's click target, so `e.target === dialog` is only true when the padding-less backdrop itself was hit. `method="dialog"` closes the form's dialog without submitting or reloading, and the return value is available via `dialog.returnValue`.

