```css
/* If self-hosting, you control font-display yourself */
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Inter';
  src: url('/fonts/inter.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-display: swap;
}
```

Why it works: the value controls the font block period — how long the browser hides text while waiting for the webfont. block waits up to ~3s with invisible text (FOIT, bad for content), swap shows the fallback instantly and swaps when ready (brief FOUT, best for reading), optional gives the font an extremely short window (~100ms) and never swaps after first paint, so the user may see the fallback for the whole page view but there is zero layout shift after render. For a content site use swap: text is never invisible, which matters most for LCP and readability.

repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)) creates as many ≥240px columns as fit, letting each grow equally. auto-fit collapses empty tracks, so with one card it stretches full width; auto-fill keeps empty tracks reserved.

